ection polls or expert ratings, or a shift in the national environment, could quickly move this race off the tossup line.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Virginia enters the 2028 presidential race with a modest Democratic tilt and very little hard evidence either way. The state's recent partisan lean favors Democrats by about three points, and the term-limited Republican incumbent leaves an open field, removing the usual incumbency boost. No general-election polls, expert ratings, or market prices exist yet, so the forecast rests almost entirely on fundamentals.\n\nDemocrats hold the governor's office under Abigail Spanberger, a sign of continued party strength in statewide races, though a recent conservative critique of her coalition hints at vulnerabilities. With more than a year until Election Day and no polling to narrow the range, the race sits at the edge of tossup territory, leaning slightly Democratic on the state's underlying partisanship alone.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6351, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6229, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6055, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6063, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6125, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6095, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6104, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6128, "margin": 3.0}]}